[
 {
  "id": 520,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_15",
  "en": "Initial observation:\nIt appeared following the successful opening of the first Gate, as the child was brought up the steps.\n\nProperties:\nEthereal webbing, mucus-like to the touch, yet doesn't easily give way. Shares certain aspects with the blood of the gods.\n\nSecondhand account:\nA yet-uncategorized sample of fauna is claimed to have been spotted within our halls. We have sealed the lower shaft. Such a presence must be investigated.\n\nPersonal account:\nUnbelievable. It is as I theorized. The glowing mycelium flows with the vibrations of the Void. Even as it writhes before my eyes, it is difficult to reconcile the Ichor as a separate form of life."
 },
 {
  "id": 521,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_16_title",
  "en": "The Mechanism"
 },
 {
  "id": 522,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_16",
  "en": "Only I remain. The stone sunders every tool. To think we ventured this far into the passageways, only to meet our end in ignorance.\n\nThe mechanism reaches through the stone. Its design is unlike any I've seen. I can only imagine it to be the work of an artificer of old.\n\nWhat a waste."
 },
 {
  "id": 523,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_17_title",
  "en": "Dear Child"
 },
 {
  "id": 524,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_17",
  "en": "My fragile light. I spit on the divines that saw fit to shape you so. I curse your fate. \n\nMay you rest within the crimson depths. May you find me again through the Salt."
 },
 {
  "id": 525,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_18_title",
  "en": "I saw it"
 },
 {
  "id": 526,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_18",
  "en": "Mother says not to speak lies, but I saw it.\n\nIt was looking at the murals. It didn't look like Mom or Dad. It looked like one of the old statues. Its skin shimmered in green. It was pretty.\n\nI hid. I touched it, and my hand turned cold. It hasn't come back again. I don't think it liked me.\n\nMy fingers feel strange now. Slimy. They don't look like mine anymore."
 },
 {
  "id": 527,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_19_title",
  "en": "The monoliths"
 },
 {
  "id": 528,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_19",
  "en": "The accursed ice is unending. We climbed further this time, yet could still not reach beyond its domain. Some did not return. They became one with the ice, circling one of the primeval monoliths.\n\nA death rite was performed in haste, as such a place does not abide the living for long. As I prepared to descend, something beckoned me to turn back towards the stone. Through the white haze, I could swear I felt their frozen eyes meet mine."
 },
 {
  "id": 529,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_20_title",
  "en": "It crawled"
 },
 {
  "id": 530,
  "ctx": "term Data/journal_entry_20",
  "en": "I dare not leave my home, for there is a change in the air. One of the gods no longer appears to the people, and the City's fonts have begun to run dry. At least that's what they say. \n\nAt night, I gaze above, greeted by shimmering colors dancing across the darkness. The stars themselves appear in motion. What does it all mean?\n\nToday I retched, hurling divine Ichor onto the floor. It sizzled on the stone. Before I could regain my wits, I was struck frozen by equal surprise and terror. The shimmering mass began to crawl."
 },
 {
  "id": 531,
  "ctx": "term Data/COMPENDIUM JOURNAL ENTRIES - LORE STONES",
  "en": "These should contain the same text (condensed into one long paragraph) as the Lore Stones on the Dialogue page (600-717)"
 },
